<urn:atm:triage:finding/AT1-QA-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AT1-QA-002" ;
  triage:title "Sprint-doc frontmatter status:complete contradicts pending publish legs per phase README status-flip convention" ;
  triage:description "docs/plans/phase-at/AT.1-install-parity-and-publish.md frontmatter sets status: complete while the AT.1 receipt records testpypi: pending-authorization-and-merge and production: pending-contemporaneous-authorization. The phase README's status-flip convention says the sprint doc must not be flipped to complete while publish legs remain pending. Fix: set the frontmatter status to the README-sanctioned intermediate value (follow the README convention exactly) until the publish legs land. Reported by req-qa, confirmed by quality-mgr in AT1-QA-R1. Full report: PR #1044 comment 5433210488." ;
